From d8568201cb937a985ffd4520dc81c12f341b73e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Mausberg <sam@findtensor.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 03:16:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add a bit-exact tensor tap for divergence forensics

With SGLANG_STATE_TAP_DIR set, forward hooks on the target model, plus
explicit taps after the GDN causal convolution and recurrence, hash the
exact bits of every output one row per token into static buffers. The
hashes are captured into CUDA graphs and replayed with them. Before each
target forward that contains a request whose rid starts with
SGLANG_STATE_TAP_RID_PREFIX (default tap-), the caches it will read are
hashed too (KV per cached position and attention layer through the
request's req_to_token row; GDN convolution and SSM state per layer).
After the forward, the request's rows are saved with the head input and
the logits fed to argmax. SGLANG_STATE_TAP_PERTURB=<module> adds one unit
in the last place to the first element of that output in every forward,
as a positive control. Off unless SGLANG_STATE_TAP_DIR is set.
